// spec: EXP-014, VAR-017
//
// ⚠️ A defect is a statement about the INTERPRETER and is never compiled.
// Whether the compiler shares the fault says nothing about whether the
// interpreter still has it.
//
// A parameter is an assignment context [VAR-017], so a Char widens to a String
// parameter and this must print 'string only'.  No widening is applied, so no
// overload fits.

class N;
begin
    function Only (S : String); begin Exit 'string only'; end
end

WriteLn (N ().Only ('a'));
